{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint add(int x, int y) {\n    x += y;\n    return x >= MOD ? x - MOD : x;\n}\n\nint mul(int x, int y) {\n    return (ll)x * y % MOD;\n}\n\nint pow_mod(int b, int e) {\n    int r = 1;\n    for (; e; e >>= 1, b = mul(b, b))\n        if (e & 1) r = mul(r, b);\n    return r;\n}\n\nint log_arr[1000001];\n\nint bsgs(int a, int m) {\n    memset(log_arr, -1, sizeof log_arr);\n    int s = (int)sqrt(m);\n    int cur = 1;\n    int inv_a = pow_mod(a, m - 2);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= s; ++i) {\n        if (log_arr[cur] == -1) log_arr[cur] = i;\n        cur = mul(cur, inv_a);\n        if (cur == 1) return i + 1;\n    }\n    \n    int step = pow_mod(a, s);\n    cur = step;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= s; ++i) {\n        if (log_arr[cur] != -1) return s * i + log_arr[cur];\n        cur = mul(cur, step);\n    }\n    \n    return -1;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n    \n    if (k == 1) {\n        cout << pow_mod(p, p);\n    } else if (k == 0) {\n        cout << pow_mod(p, p - 1);\n    } else {\n        int d = bsgs(k, p);\n        cout << pow_mod(p, (p - 1) / d);\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static int[] log_arr = new int[1000001];\n\n    static int add(int x, int y) {\n        x += y;\n        return x >= MOD ? x - MOD : x;\n    }\n\n    static int mul(int x, int y) {\n        return (int) (((long) x * y) % MOD);\n    }\n\n    static int pow_mod(int b, int e) {\n        int r = 1;\n        for (; e > 0; e >>= 1, b = mul(b, b)) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) r = mul(r, b);\n        }\n        return r;\n    }\n\n    static int bsgs(int a, int m) {\n        Arrays.fill(log_arr, -1);\n        int s = (int) Math.sqrt(m);\n        int cur = 1;\n        int inv_a = pow_mod(a, m - 2);\n\n        for (int i = 0; i <= s; ++i) {\n            if (log_arr[cur] == -1) log_arr[cur] = i;\n            cur = mul(cur, inv_a);\n            if (cur == 1) return i + 1;\n        }\n\n        int step = pow_mod(a, s);\n        cur = step;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= s; ++i) {\n            if (log_arr[cur] != -1) return s * i + log_arr[cur];\n            cur = mul(cur, step);\n        }\n\n        return -1;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int p = scanner.nextInt();\n        int k = scanner.nextInt();\n\n        if (k == 1) {\n            System.out.println(pow_mod(p, p));\n        } else if (k == 0) {\n            System.out.println(pow_mod(p, p - 1));\n        } else {\n            int d = bsgs(k, p);\n            System.out.println(pow_mod(p, (p - 1) / d));\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001523378741694614